@title Crane model: pick a STEP crane of your own, see it in place of the generic crane, change a role, undo
@area Simulate
# Hoist in 3D shows a generic crane. "Crane model..." asks for a STEP file (the synthetic workshop crane
# here); the picture then shows the file's solids, coloured by role. Parts lists the solids with the role
# guessed from each name; changing one is kept in the project. Edit > Undo takes the pick back.
open qa/fixtures/travel-drive.novo
wait 20
key ctrl+k
wait 3
text Hoist in 3D
wait 4
key Enter
wait 30
shot generic-crane
expect "Crane model…"
expect_not "Parts"
answer_dialog qa/fixtures/crane-model/workshop-crane.stp
click_text "Crane model…"
wait 120
expect_dialog "crane model"
expect "workshop-crane.stp"
expect "Generic crane"
expect_not "Runway"
shot own-crane
check_layout
click_text "Parts"
wait 30
expect "Crane model parts"
expect "23 parts"
expect "Runway support A"
shot parts-window
check_layout
check_text 20
# Pointing at a row paints that solid in the picture.
move 130 250
wait 20
shot pointing-at-a-row
move 700 700
wait 10
# The first solid is a runway support (role other, yellow). Make it a girder: it turns blue in the picture.
click_text "other"
wait 10
shot role-menu
click_text "girder" #2
wait 30
expect "Guess from names"
expect_enabled "Guess from names"
shot role-changed
click_text "Guess from names"
wait 30
expect_disabled "Guess from names"
shot roles-guessed
# Y up lays the model on its side.
click_text "Z"
wait 10
click_text "Y"
wait 30
shot y-up
click_text "Y"
wait 10
click_text "Z"
wait 30
click_text "Generic crane"
wait 40
expect "Runway"
expect_not "workshop-crane.stp"
shot back-to-generic
